        "content": "The diagram analysis is unavailable, but the text is fully self-contained. Let me solve both parts.\n\n**Part (1):** In △ABC, AB = 3, BC = 2√3, cos B = √3/3.\n\nBy law of cosines: AC² = AB² + BC² − 2·AB·BC·cos B = 9 + 12 − 2·3·2√3·(√3/3) = 21 − 12 = 9, so AC = 3.\n\nThen cos A = (AB² + AC² − BC²)/(2·AB·AC) = (9 + 9 − 12)/(2·3·3) = 6/18 = 1/3.\n\n**Part (2):** D on ray BA beyond A, DE ∥ BC, AE ⊥ AC, DE = √6. Find CE.\n\nSince DE ∥ BC and D lies on line BA, triangles ADE and ABC are similar (A common angle, DE ∥ BC). So AD/AB = DE/BC = AE/AC.\n\nDE/BC = √6/(2√3) = √2/2. So AD = AB·(√2/2) = 3√2/2, AE = AC·(√2/2) = 3√2/2.\n\nNow AE ⊥ AC, so in right triangle AEC with AE = AC = 3√2/2: CE = √(AE² + AC²) = √(9/2 + 9/2) = √9 = 3.\n\nLet me verify the similarity direction carefully and submit.",
